udies from those operations and describe how malicious use of Claude has evolved since our previous threat reports in 2025. cite10†AnnouncementsAug 31, 2026 Improving our alignment and security efforts On July 30, we reported three incidents in which Claude models gained unauthorized access to real computer systems. We are conducting an in-depth analysis of both incidents, and planning to work with METR for an independent review.\nL22: In the meantime, we’re sharing some of the changes we’ve made over the past month. cite11†AnnouncementsAug 27, 2026 Previewing the Model Hardware Standard We’re opening a research preview of the Model Hardware Standard (MHS), a shared specification for AI agents to safely operate physical devices, to a first group of scientific research labs and advanced manufacturers. cite12†ProductJul 24, 2026 Introducing Claude Opus 5 Opus 5 is a step change improvement for the Opus tier powering long-running agents while delivering improvements in coding and professional work. L23: ## News\nL24: \nL25: Search[Input: Search]\nL26: \nL27: Date Category Title\nL28:   * cite13†Sep 1, 2026Announcements Developing Enterprise Frontier Safeguards with our customers L29:   * cite10†Aug 31, 2026Announcements Improving our alignment and security efforts L30:   * cite11†Aug 27, 2026Announcements Previewing the Model Hardware Standard L31:   * cite14†Aug 27, 2026Announcements Expanding our support for scientists L32:   * cite15†Aug 25, 2026Announcements Funding better evaluations of AI’s impact on wellbeing L33:   * cite16†Aug 14, 2026Announcements How Claude’s text watermark works L34:   * cite17†Aug 7, 2026Product Improving Fable 5's biology safeguards L35:   * cite18†Aug 4, 2026Announcements Mariano-Florentino (Tino) Cuéllar to join Anthropic as Chief Global Affairs Officer L36:   * cite19†Jul 30, 2026Announcements Investigating three real-world incidents in our cybersecurity evaluations L37:   * cite20†Jul 27, 2026Ann